  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The decrease in mass  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></math>  will appear as the kinetic energy of the two daughter nuclei. Since the two nuclei formed are of equal masses, they will share the available energy equally among themselves. If  <math><mi>v</mi></math>  is the speed of a daughter nucleus, then  <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>or     <math><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi>c</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
